<http://data.silknow.org/object/25b86deb-a3c1-3202-a53c-43c251cda7fd>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "embroidered, 1770-1850, Persian; Whitework"@en , "Cotton padded and quilted with silk in running stitch, bound with woven wool; whitework. \nDisplayed behind glass.\nFour curving triangular panels of white cotton joined together to form a pointed hat. There is a border of joined diamonds along the three sides of each panel.  Within this there is a pattern of bands at the bottom of each panel with everything worked in white silk:\n[1] impossible to see the design\n[2] zigzag line\n[3] left bending boetehs\n[4] as [2]\n[5] as [1]\nThe remaining triangular field is filled with a fine pattern of stems and flowers.\nBinding/Facing: stripe wool: red, white and blue stripes each with a decorative pattern."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/5180d196-706d-3382-9c21-202f2f843e89> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/9e3e1ec3-59c3-35f5-a2d3-081d8ce718b0> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "embroidered, 1770-1850, Persian; Whitework"@en , "Cotton padded and quilted with silk in running stitch, bound with woven wool; whitework. \nDisplayed behind glass.\nFour curving triangular panels of white cotton joined together to form a pointed hat. There is a border of joined diamonds along the three sides of each panel.  Within this there is a pattern of bands at the bottom of each panel with everything worked in white silk:\n[1] impossible to see the design\n[2] zigzag line\n[3] left bending boetehs\n[4] as [2]\n[5] as [1]\nThe remaining triangular field is filled with a fine pattern of stems and flowers.\nBinding/Facing: stripe wool: red, white and blue stripes each with a decorative pattern."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/25b86deb-a3c1-3202-a53c-43c251cda7fd/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/25b86deb-a3c1-3202-a53c-43c251cda7fd/dimension/2> ;
